Rem ==================================================================
Rem seq.shoddy — Shoddy standard library: sequences
Rem The usual Fold/Map suspects. Pure, self-hosted. Structure only:
Rem predicates, searching, slicing, zipping — aggregation (Sum, Mean,
Rem and friends) lives in stats.shoddy.
Rem
Rem Built on the nineteen sequence and higher-order builtins, each
Rem documented one by one immediately below: Map Filter Fold Each Times
Rem Range, and Length Reverse Concat Sort IsEmpty First Nth SetNth Dim
Rem ToArray ToList Rest Prepend. Sorting is the Sort builtin and is
Rem documented here too, though stats.shoddy is its heaviest caller.
Rem
Rem Words marked (poly) work on LISTs and ARRAYs; others are List-only
Rem because they lean on First/Rest/Prepend structural recursion.
Rem ==================================================================

Rem ---- the builtins this machine is built on -------------------------
Rem
Rem NOT Defs. The engine dispatches these, and a Def whose name is a
Rem builtin is refused; they are written here because seq.shoddy is
Rem where a reader goes looking for them. The flat reference is section
Rem 10 of docs/spec.html, and the stack effects below are the ones the
Rem compiler's own Effects.cs table declares.
Rem
Rem TWO SEQUENCE KINDS, AND THE DIFFERENCE IS THE WHOLE DESIGN. A LIST
Rem is a linked list: First and Rest are free, Nth walks. An ARRAY is
Rem contiguous: Nth is O(1), and Rest would have to copy. Recurse over
Rem lists; index into arrays; ToArray and ToList convert. Everything
Rem here counts from 1.
Rem
Rem ALL NINETEEN ARE PURE, including SetNth — it answers a NEW sequence
Rem and leaves the original alone, which is what makes them safe to
Rem share.

Rem ---- higher-order ----

Rem Map(xs As List Of t, f As [ t -- u ]) As List Of u
Rem                                                   ( xs f -- ys )
Rem     Every element through f. Poly: an array maps to an array.

Rem Filter(xs As List Of t, p As [ t -- Boolean ]) As List Of t
Rem                                                   ( xs p -- ys )
Rem     The elements p answers True for, in order.

Rem Fold(xs As List Of t, init As u, f As [ u t -- u ]) As u
Rem                                                   ( xs init f -- v )
Rem     Left fold: the accumulator starts at init and f sees it first.
Rem     Almost every word below this header is Fold underneath.

Rem Each(xs As List Of t, f As [ t -- ])              ( xs f -- )
Rem     f applied to every element for its EFFECT, answering nothing.
Rem     The one word in this group that exists only for impure work.

Rem Times(n As Number, f As [ Number -- ])            ( n f -- )
Rem     f applied to 1, 2, … n, for effect. The counted loop.

Rem Range(lo As Number, hi As Number) As List Of Number
Rem                                                   ( lo hi -- xs )
Rem     The whole numbers from lo to hi inclusive. An empty list when hi
Rem     is below lo, so a loop over an empty range simply does nothing.

Rem ---- asking about a sequence ----

Rem Length(xs As List Of t) As Number                 ( xs -- n )
Rem     How many elements. LIST-AND-ARRAY ONLY — it REFUSES a string
Rem     outright, which is why Len (str.shoddy's) is a separate word and
Rem     not a near miss for this one.

Rem IsEmpty(xs As List Of t) As Boolean               ( xs -- flag )
Rem     Whether it holds nothing.

Rem First(xs As List Of t) As t                       ( xs -- v )
Rem     The first element. Aborts on an empty sequence.

Rem Rest(xs As List Of t) As List Of t                ( xs -- ys )
Rem     Everything after the first. LISTS ONLY: on an array it would
Rem     have to copy, and the point of an array is that it does not.

Rem Nth(xs As List Of t, k As Number) As t            ( xs k -- v )
Rem     The k-th element, counting from 1. Aborts outside the range.
Rem     O(1) on an array, a walk on a list.

Rem ---- building a new one ----

Rem Prepend(v As t, xs As List Of t) As List Of t     ( v xs -- ys )
Rem     xs with v on the front. LISTS ONLY, and free — this is the pair
Rem     to First/Rest that structural recursion is written with.

Rem SetNth(xs As List Of t, k As Number, v As t) As List Of t
Rem                                                   ( xs k v -- ys )
Rem     A sequence with its k-th element replaced. THE ORIGINAL IS
Rem     UNCHANGED. Aborts outside the range.

Rem Reverse(xs As List Of t) As List Of t             ( xs -- ys )
Rem     The same elements, back to front.

Rem Concat(xs As List Of t, ys As List Of t) As List Of t
Rem                                                   ( xs ys -- zs )
Rem     The two joined. Append and Flatten below are written over it.

Rem Sort(xs As List Of t) As List Of t                ( xs -- ys )
Rem     Ascending, over all-numbers or all-strings. Mixed kinds have no
Rem     order and are refused. It is a sequence operation and so it is
Rem     documented here, though stats.shoddy is its heaviest caller —
Rem     every median, quantile and rank goes through it.

Rem Dim(n As Number, init As t) As Array Of t         ( n init -- arr )
Rem     An ARRAY of n copies of init. The way an array is made, since
Rem     there is no array literal.

Rem ToArray(xs As List Of t) As Array Of t            ( xs -- arr )
Rem ToList(arr As Array Of t) As List Of t            ( arr -- xs )
Rem     Between the two kinds. The usual shape is: build with list
Rem     recursion, ToArray once, then index.

Rem ---- this machine's own words --------------------------------------

Rem ---- predicates over sequences (poly) ------------------------------

Def Any(xs As List Of t, p As [ t -- Boolean ]) As Boolean
    Fold(xs, False, Fn(a, x) => a Or Call(p, x))

Def All(xs As List Of t, p As [ t -- Boolean ]) As Boolean
    Fold(xs, True, Fn(a, x) => a And Call(p, x))

Def CountIf(xs As List Of t, p As [ t -- Boolean ]) As Number
    Length(Filter(xs, p))

Def Contains(xs As List Of t, v As t) As Boolean
    Any(xs, =(v))

Rem ---- searching (List) ----------------------------------------------

Def IndexFrom(xs As List Of t, v As t, k As Number) As Number
    If IsEmpty(xs) Then
        0
    Else
        If First(xs) = v Then
            k
        Else
            IndexFrom(Rest(xs), v, k + 1)

Rem Zero for "not there" — indices are 1-based, so 0 is a position that
Rem cannot occur and the sentinel is at least unambiguous. IndexOpt is the
Rem honest word and the one to reach for in new code; this pair keeps its
Rem shape because too much of the tree already reads the 0.
Def IndexOf(xs As List Of t, v As t) As Number
    IndexFrom(xs, v, 1)

Rem The same search, saying "absent" in the language's own words instead of
Rem in a number that has to be remembered. Option needs no Include — it is
Rem the language's, so a caller matching on this pulls in nothing.
Def IndexOpt(xs As List Of t, v As t) As Option
    Let k = IndexFrom(xs, v, 1)
    If k = 0 Then
        None()
    Else
        Some(k)

Rem ---- slicing and building (List) -----------------------------------

Def Taken(xs As List Of t, n As Number) As List Of t
    If n <= 0 Or IsEmpty(xs) Then
        { }
    Else
        Prepend(First(xs), Taken(Rest(xs), n - 1))

Def DropN(xs As List Of t, n As Number) As List Of t
    If n <= 0 Or IsEmpty(xs) Then
        xs
    Else
        DropN(Rest(xs), n - 1)

Def Append(xs As List Of t, x As t) As List Of t
    Concat(xs, { x })

Def Last(xs As List Of t) As t
    Nth(xs, Length(xs))

Def Flatten(xss As List Of List Of t) As List Of t
    Fold(xss, { }, Concat)

Rem ---- pairing --------------------------------------------------------

Type Pair
    Fst As t
    Snd As u

Def ZipWith(xs As List Of t, ys As List Of u, f As [ t u -- v ]) As List Of v
    Map(Range(1, Min(Length(xs), Length(ys))), Fn(k) => Call(f, Nth(xs, k), Nth(ys, k)))

Def Zip(xs As List Of t, ys As List Of u) As List Of Pair
    ZipWith(xs, ys, Pair)
